1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,310
Nvidia just dropped twelve point nine billion on Hugging Face. Anthropic wants thirty trillion. And OpenAI just fired Cursor. All in one week.

2
00:00:06,310 --> 00:00:14,060
Nvidia agreed to acquire Hugging Face for twelve point nine billion dollars. That's nearly double HF's last valuation. Jensen Huang now controls the platform hosting half the world's open models.

3
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:25,780
Speaking of open models — Z.ai just dropped GLM-5.3-Flash. Three hundred twenty billion total parameters, eighteen billion active. MIT license. Ten times more cost-efficient than its predecessor. The stealth Ox Alpha model is now public.

4
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:34,660
Meanwhile Anthropic is pitching IPO investors a thirty trillion dollar total addressable market. That's nearly forty percent of the entire US stock market. They're targeting a two trillion valuation and a hundred billion dollar raise.

5
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:43,690
Google answered with Gemini 3.5 Transcribe. Two point six percent word error rate across eighty-five languages. Separate APIs for streaming and batch. It even deletes your ums and ahs automatically.

6
00:00:43,690 --> 00:00:53,330
Which brings us to trust. DeepMind just ran the first double-blind evaluation of a frontier Gemini model. External testers can't see weights. Google can't see prompts. Confidential computing eliminates benchmark contamination.

7
00:00:53,330 --> 00:01:01,160
And Anthropic made Sonnet 5's intro pricing permanent. Two dollars input, ten dollars output per million tokens. The three-fifteen standard rate scheduled for September first? Gone.

8
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:10,240
But the week's sharpest turn — OpenAI cutting off Cursor after SpaceX's sixty billion dollar takeover. November twelfth shutdown. Cursor says it's five percent of traffic. Anthropic and Google just gained a massive opening.

9
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:13,190
